USAGE

##Package Installation Playbook
---
- name: Install required packages
  hosts: linux_servers
  become: true

  tasks:
    - name: Install packages
      ansible.builtin.dnf:
        name:
          - vim
          - curl
          - wget
        state: present

Run:

ansible-playbook -i inventory/dev.ini playbooks/install_packages.yml


##Create Directory

---
- name: Create application directory
  hosts: linux_servers
  become: true

  tasks:
    - name: Ensure application directory exists
      ansible.builtin.file:
        path: /opt/application
        state: directory
        owner: root
        group: root
        mode: '0755'


##Manage Service

---
- name: Configure HTTP service
  hosts: linux_servers
  become: true

  tasks:
    - name: Install Apache
      ansible.builtin.dnf:
        name: httpd
        state: present

    - name: Start Apache
      ansible.builtin.service:
        name: httpd
        state: started
        enabled: true


##Server Patching

---
- name: Patch Linux servers
  hosts: linux_servers
  become: true
  serial: 1

  tasks:
    - name: Update installed packages
      ansible.builtin.dnf:
        name: "*"
        state: latest

In production environments, patch procedures should include:

Pre-check
Backup/Snapshot
Application owner approval
Maintenance window
Patch deployment
Reboot decision
Post-check
Monitoring validation
Rollback plan
